From 924e9f702627d6a456c953dc77f2b565e017fdbe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CipherScope <dev@cipherscope.io>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 09:19:59 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] test: add feature_signet_pqblock_edges.py

Three edge cases of -signetpqblock on an OP_TRUE signet.

A pruned node that accepted a block without the signature before it got the
rule fails the block check at startup and cannot use -reindex-chainstate;
-reindex marks the block invalid, and the node then takes the valid chain
from a peer. A signet node prunes nothing below height 1000, so its block
files still hold every block.

A signed block of exactly the maximum weight is accepted and one weight unit
heavier is rejected with bad-blk-weight: the PQ push is non-witness data.

A copy of a signed block that changes only a witness (the coinbase's witness
reserved value, or a transaction's witness) keeps the block's hash and a
valid signature: transactions enter the signature's message only through
their txids. The node rejects the copy as mutated without marking the hash
invalid, and accepts the block afterwards. A copy with another PQ push fails
the merkle root check before the signature is checked.
